 ### BVH-based UDF evaluation with analytic gradient
-Computes the unsigned distance from query points to a triangle mesh using a BVH, and provides an analytic gradient for backpropagation [S8, unofficial].
-*   **Forward:** Flatten input $x$ to $[N, 3]$. Query BVH for distance `udf`, triangle ID `tri_id`, and barycentric coordinates `uvw`. Clamp `uvw` to $[10^{-9}, 1-10^{-9}]$. Interpolate nearest point on triangle using `uvw` and triangle vertices. Return `udf` reshaped to input shape [S8, unofficial].
-*   **Backward:** Retrieve saved $x$ and `nearest_points`. Compute `diff = x - nearest_points`. Compute `norm = diff.norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True) + 10^{-8}`. Gradient is `grad_output` scaled by `diff/norm` [S8, unofficial].
-*   **Formula:** $\nabla_x \text{UDF}(x) = \frac{x - p_{\text{nearest}}}{\|x - p_{\text{nearest}}\|}$ where $p_{\text{nearest}}$ is the closest point on the mesh [S8, unofficial].
-*   **Pitfall:** `uvw` is clamped to $[10^{-9}, 1-10^{-9}]$ to avoid invalid barycentric coordinates at triangle edges/corners [S8, unofficial].
